1.15.0: the filter rack - Wratten contrast filters before the film

--filter yellow|orange|red|green|blue on polajuice and superjuice,
FILTER= in super8ify, a dropdown on the page: per-channel transmittance
applied to the light before the film integrates it, exposure
renormalized by the filter factor. Orange+bw darkens skies and pops
clouds, red is the violent version, green lightens foliage; on color
stock it is the period cast it always was. Works with measured cubes
(the emulsion sees filtered light, as in life) and the scalar engine
alike. Unknown filters refused with the rack named. Core test proves
yellow < none and red < yellow on a blue sky through bw; movie, wasm
and DOM suites cover their layers. Wratten triplets stylized from
published band curves, disclosed in PRESET_SOURCES.
